			"type": "text",
			"text": "Colossosuchus was a phytosaur from the Upper Triassic Tiki Formation of India. Its name comes from 'Collosus' a Greek word used for giants and 'suchus' meaning crocodile. The animal was the biggest of its relatives at 8 meters long. It had a dome like skull and down curved tip at the end of its upper jaw. The remains of the animal were found alongside many others of its species, amounting to -at minimum- 21 individuals, mostly juveniles and sub-adults."
